+## Subtopics
+
+### Iso-Crossing Detection
+Similar to zeroCrossing but detects crossings of a specified iso-value. It uses an HDDA for empty-space ray-marching. If an intersection with the iso-surface is detected, it updates `ijk`, `v`, and `t`. The logic is identical to zero-crossing but compares `acc.getValue(ijk) - iso` against zero [S4, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Depends on the depth of the tree and the density of the narrow band. HDDA allows skipping empty space efficiently.
-- **Memory Complexity:** Minimal additional memory per ray; uses cache hints to optimize L1/L2 usage [S2, unofficial].
-- **Performance:** On RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, 1M rays, dragon dataset (267 MB SDF), fp32, eps=0: Speedup 1.95x (1.263ms -> 0.646ms). Instructions reduced by 50.6% (1.29e+08 -> 6.35e+07). Registers reduced from 80 to 78 [S2, unofficial]. On emu dataset (1.0 GB SDF): Speedup 1.73x. On crawler dataset (1.6 GB SDF): Speedup 1.67x [S2, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** High performance due to leaf-only traversal and cache hints. Correctness for inside-surface rays and disjoint regions.
-- **Limitations:** Requires HDDA infrastructure. FP16 support requires careful arithmetic handling [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Depends on the number of active voxels along the ray and the depth of the tree. HDDA allows skipping empty space efficiently.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Low, primarily storing ray state and HDDA state per thread.
+*   **Performance:** On RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, 1M rays, dragon dataset (267 MB SDF), fp32, eps=0: Speedup 1.95x (1.263ms -> 0.646ms). Instructions reduced by 50.6% (1.29e+08 -> 6.35e+07). Registers reduced from 80 to 78 [S2, unofficial]. On emu dataset (1.0 GB SDF): Speedup 1.73x (1.832ms -> 1.059ms). On crawler dataset (1.6 GB SDF): Speedup 1.67x (3.586ms -> 2.143ms) [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths:** High performance due to tile-skipping and cache-hint optimizations. Correctness for rays starting inside the surface. Support for fp16 inputs [S2, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** L1 hit rate dips (94.5 → 87.8 on dragon) due to streaming-store path bypassing L1 and tile-skipping removing trivially cache-friendly reads [S2, unofficial]. Instruction count rises on uniform_ray_samples count pass (+8.2% dragon) even as cycles fall [S2, unofficial].
+*   **When to Use:** When high-performance SDF ray intersection is needed, especially for large grids with sparse active regions. When rays may start inside the surface. When fp16 support is required [S2, unofficial].
+*   **When Not to Use:** When exact iso-value crossing is needed (use Iso-Crossing Detection). When grid contains active coarse tiles that must be processed per-voxel (use HDDAActiveValueIterator) [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-Originated in the OpenVDB/fvdb-core project, specifically in the `ray_implicit_intersection` kernel optimization [S2, unofficial]. It is based on the `nanovdb::ZeroCrossing` method [S1]. The method was improved to fix correctness issues and enhance performance by reorganizing HDDA iterators and adding cache hints [S2, unofficial].
+Originated in OpenVDB/nanovdb as `nanovdb::ZeroCrossing` and `nanovdb::ZeroCrossingNode` [S1]. Optimized and hardened in fvdb-core as `ray_implicit_intersection` [S2, unofficial]. Used in volume rendering and implicit surface raycasting [S3, unofficial].
 
